    <article class="panel-card">
      <h2>What Spectra EQ does</h2>
      <p>Spectra EQ is Stackdrop’s desktop equalizer. The top of the window is a live spectrum of what is playing. The bottom is a 10-band EQ from 20 Hz through 10 kHz, plus preamp and master. Each band has a knob and a slider. Hover any control for a tooltip. Scroll for 1 dB. Right-click a band to set it back to 0.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Presets for Flat, Bass Boost, Treble, V-Shape, Vocal, Electronic, Rock, Classical, Podcast, Cinema, Night, and Loudness</li>
        <li>System-wide EQ after you install Equalizer APO once and reboot</li>
        <li>Runs locally. No account. No ads.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="panel-card">
      <h2>Make it change all sound</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Download Spectra EQ and <a href="/downloads/EqualizerAPO.exe">Equalizer APO</a>. Open Spectra. The spectrum should move when music plays.</li>
        <li>Install Equalizer APO, tick your Speakers, and reboot. Windows has to install it separately. It does not come inside Spectra EQ.</li>
        <li>Open Spectra EQ again, press <strong>EQ ON</strong>, and move a slider. YouTube, games, and other playback follow the curve.</li>
        <li>Press <strong>EQ OFF</strong> to return the sound to flat.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Equalizer APO is the Windows audio effect. <a href="/downloads/EqualizerAPO.exe">Download Equalizer APO</a> (official 1.4.2, 64-bit), install it, tick Speakers, and reboot. The driver cannot be hidden inside Spectra itself.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="panel-card">
      <h2>Build it yourself</h2>
      <p>The source download includes <code>Eq.py</code> and <code>build_exe.bat</code>. On Windows, put them in the same folder and run <code>build_exe.bat</code>. The window title should say <strong>2.6.18-drag</strong>. Replace <code>SpectraEQ.exe</code> in the equalizer folder so the download button serves the new build. Equalizer APO stays a separate download.</p>
